  "worked_solution": "We rearrange the terms so that the like terms, $13x$ and $5x$, are together.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13x-2y+5x+1 & = \\\\ {{13x+5x}_{⏟}}_{x\\text{ terms}}-2y+1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{13x+5x}_{⏟}-2y+1 & = \\\\ (13+5)x-2y+1 & = \\\\ 18x-2y+1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
